    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. it sounds like the FLN really had the moral and strategic high ground there. since i'm focusing on the struggle, can you elaborate on why the French military's counter-measures were essentially just failed attempts to suppress a legitimate liberation movement? like, was there any legitimate way for the colonial government to respond that wasn't just violent repression?",
